<article class="legal wrap wrap--narrow">
  <h1>Terms of service</h1>
  <p class="legal__date">Last updated 12 November 2026</p>

  <p>
    These terms cover the hosted pux service at pux.vidur.xyz and the pux apps, run by Vidur Butalia. By using them you agree to these terms. If you run your own server, these terms don't apply to it, and the
    <a href="https://github.com/vidurb/pux/blob/main/LICENSE">AGPL-3.0 licence</a>
    governs your use of the source code.
  </p>

  <h2>What pux is</h2>
  <p>
    pux receives emails you forward to it, looks for a one-time code and sends it to your devices in encrypted form. It isn't a bank, it isn't affiliated with any bank, and it doesn't replace your bank's own way of delivering codes.
  </p>

  <h2>Don't rely on it alone</h2>
  <p>
    pux is an early release and delivery isn't guaranteed. Codes can be delayed or lost: push services may hold messages, undelivered pushes expire, emails may not parse, and rate limits can drop mail. Keep another way of receiving your codes. A sender shown as verified means its DKIM signature checked out, not that the message was meant for you, so check that a code matches something you just did.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be at least 18 to use pux.</li>
    <li>
      Only forward mail you're entitled to forward, and check that doing so is allowed by your bank and your email provider.
    </li>
    <li>
      Keep your enrollment QR code and JSON export private. Anyone who has them can read your relay's codes.
    </li>
    <li>We can't recover your keys. If you lose them, create a new relay.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Don't use the service to intercept anyone else's codes, send spam or abusive mail, disrupt the service or get around its limits. Security research is welcome under our <a href="https://github.com/vidurb/pux/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>. We may rate-limit or remove relays that break these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We can change, suspend or stop the hosted service at any time. A device is removed after 2 years with no app open and no code delivered, and a relay is deleted automatically 30 days after it loses its last device. We'll post changes to these terms on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty and limit of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service and apps are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for losses arising from using them, including missed or delayed codes, or locked or compromised accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts of the National Capital Territory of Delhi have jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:privacy@vidur.xyz">privacy@vidur.xyz</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</article>
